WEBVTT

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:03.870
<i>It's the last hand of the first half 
of the third players' match</i>

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.960
<i>of the A Block semifinals 
here at the Nationals!</i>

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:07.940
<i>Shiraitodai's Shibuya Takami</i>

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.740
<i>has gotten an incredible starting hand!</i>

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:11.460
Ako...

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.110
<i>This is the last hand.</i>

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:16.490
<i>Shibuya Takami's tiles 
are really scary!</i>

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:21.750
<i>Based on her first discards so far, 
it's at least something like this.</i>

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:25.890
<i>I'll have to win as quickly as 
possible while avoiding a direct hit</i>

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:28.000
<i>and making sure not to 
discard any honor tiles</i>

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.730
<i>other than red and white dragons.</i>

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.020
In the first half, Takami only had 7 slots,

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.980
so that freshie quickly ended that one.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:40.010
This time she has eleven slots,
 so she could pull it off!

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:42.000
You're a freshie, too.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.830
Based on my skills, I'd be in 
the 100th year of high school.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:49.020
<i>Is she stupid?</i>

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.800
Third Players' Match 
 Second Half 
 South Hand 4

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:27.200
<b>Aspiration</b>

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.300
Riichi.

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:36.640
Pon.

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:40.800
<i>Crap, I made a weird noise.</i>

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:46.370
<i>Shindouji must know that Shibuya Takami</i>

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:47.810
<i>could have a yakuman hand.</i>

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:50.220
<i>That must mean that her 
hand is that good.</i>

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:55.070
<i>Oh man, why does this have to 
happen when I'm the dealer?</i>

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:56.720
<i>FunaQ said I should be wary</i>

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:58.380
<i>of something from Shibuya's side, but...</i>

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:02.660
<i>it doesn't matter if I just
 gain more than her!</i>

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:08.000
<i>She called the south and 
discarded the north,</i>

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.930
<i>which means it's like this right now.</i>

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:12.150
<i>Even the cheapest 
estimate is a haneman.</i>

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:15.550
<i>Even a toitoi with a tsumo 
would be a guaranteed sanbaiman.</i>

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:15.550
[Sanbaiman = 3x mangan = 24,000 points]
[toitoi: hand consisting of all triplets or quads, and a pair]

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:19.940
<i>Compared to that, my 
hand is really horrible.</i>

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.130
<i>Since the honor tiles are 
going to Shibuya Takami,</i>

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:24.800
<i>the range of tiles left in the
 wall should be significantly smaller.</i>

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:41.110
<i>Hatsu!</i>

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:42.390
Tsumo.

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:47.370
That's 8,000, 16,000.

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:50.120
<i>She busts out with a Daisangen!</i>

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.370
The third players' match is over!

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:55.650
<i>She got us...</i>

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:57.810
<i>Bring on the dealer penalty.</i>

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:01.960
The top point earner in this match 
is Senriyama Girls' Eguchi Sera!

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:03.430
Thanks, guys.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:12.100
Senriyama Girls' (North Osaka) 
3rd Year - Third Player
 Eguchi Sera

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:05.830
Even after the dealer's penalty

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:07.470
of the yakuman, she gained 37,000 points!

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:10.500
We can see why she was Senriyama's ace

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:12.310
as a second year student last year!

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:16.320
The next highest earner was 
Achiga Girls' Atarashi Ako!

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:20.480
Achiga Girls' (Nara) 
1st Year - Third Player 
Atarashi Ako

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:17.890
Thank you.

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:20.820
She put up a great fight, even 
though she's just a first year.

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:24.890
Following her is Shiraitodai High 
School's Shibuya Takami.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:36.210
Shiraitodai High School
 (West Tokyo)
2nd Year - Third Player
 Shibuya Takami

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:26.750
Thank... you.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.710
Even though she pulled off a Daisangen,

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:30.530
her total actually went down.

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:33.150
However, it's amazing that, 
out of the five yakumans

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:36.150
at this tournament, 
two were scored by her!

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:40.130
Shindouji's Ezaki has lost a lot of points.

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:47.510
Shindouji Girls' (Fukuoka)
3rd Year - Third Player
 Ezaki Hitomi

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:42.230
Good game...

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:44.700
She only dealt into two hands,

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:47.450
but she had quite a lot of 
points shaved off from tsumos.

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:50.100
Everything is because of bad politics!

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:51.600
Good game.

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:54.580
You were quite good today.

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:57.820
You too. Bad luck that you 
were the last dealer.

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:00.630
Well, it was better than her being it.

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:03.000
Shibuya-san?

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:07.050
Is it me or are there no records 
of her being the last dealer?

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:08.950
That's why I was afraid of it.

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:12.700
If Shibuya Takami was 
the last dealer and won,

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:15.970
how would her next hand look?

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:19.710
She'd keep winning... yakuman hands?

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:22.300
Not something we want 
to think about, right?

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:25.100
Well, let's play again soon, huh?

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:26.740
Hey, knock it off!

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:30.650
Oh, come on, this is a touching 
moment between two players.

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:32.310
I do want to play you again...

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.350
<i>but you're a bit scary 
because you're so boyish!</i>

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:38.940
<i>Damn her flirting!</i>

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:42.600
Ako-chan, you did it!

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:43.820
Ako...

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:48.700
It looks like Ako's speaking on 
friendly terms with that Eguchi Sera!

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:51.970
She speaks on friendly terms with everyone.

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:54.680
Surprisingly, until you 
become friends with her,

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:56.610
she can actually be quite reserved.

00:05:57.630 --> 00:05:58.610
Actually?

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:00.500
I guess...

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:03.040
I'll go overtake the one in second place.

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:04.280
Good luck!

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:05.290
Marvelous!

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.450
Everything is because of bad politics!

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:12.450
No, you lost those points.

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:13.640
Zero sugarcoating...

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:16.030
I was able to gain points 
in the second round match,

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:17.360
but I'm sorry about this time!

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:19.560
Well, leave it to me.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:21.650
President...

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:23.530
We're quite behind,

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:26.210
so I was thinking of raising 
the limit bar higher today.

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:29.070
I'll leave it all to you.

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:31.640
I see.

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:35.450
I'm off then.

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:38.690
Good luck, Arata-san!

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:40.220
Arata-chan, fight!

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:41.350
Good luck...

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:47.090
Arata, I'm happy that 
you're wearing that tie,

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:50.700
but don't you think it might be 
a bad omen for the semifinals?

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.360
What are you talking about, Haru-chan?

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:59.980
This tie is part of the reason 
that I am here now.

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:04.190
Therefore, I'll take it with me...
 all the way to the finals!

00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:07.150
<i>Arata...</i>

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:08.740
<i>I'm counting on you!</i>

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:14.410
All right, now there's just four 
East-South matches left!

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:14.410
Achiga Girls' (Nara)
2nd Year - Fourth Player
 Sagimori Arata

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:15.410
Shindouji Girls' (Fukuoka)
3rd Year - Fourth Player
Shirouzu Mairu

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:17.030
This is the 4th players' match 
in Block A's semifinals!

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:16.410
Senriyama Girls' (North Osaka)
2nd Year - Fourth Player
 Funakubo Hiroko

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:17.410
Shiraitodai High School (West Tokyo)
 2nd Year - Fourth Player
 Matano Seiko

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:19.020
And it begins!

00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:23.170
<i>The semifinals...</i>

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:25.850
<i>The hurdle Haru-chan 
was not able to clear...</i>

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:32.370
<i>Now, I've got to at least 
take second place here.</i>

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:36.140
<i>The biggest obstacle 
in the way of that is...</i>

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:38.340
<i>Probably Shiraitodai.</i>

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:49.390
<i>I'll scope out the situation 
during the first hand</i>

00:07:49.390 --> 00:07:51.500
<i>and won't set any limits yet.</i>

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:53.410
Pon.

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:54.160
<i>Here she goes!</i>

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:57.330
<i>She can fish up tiles 
at will from the discards.</i>

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:59.330
<i>Shiraitodai's fisher...</i>

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:02.040
<i>Matano Seiko!</i>

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:06.030
<i>Well, it's really just a normal pon...</i>

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:08.560
<i>Matano only became a regular last year,</i>

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:09.880
<i>so there aren't many records of her games.</i>

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:13.160
<i>What I was able to glean 
from those limited sources</i>

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:15.940
<i>is that she always calls 
three times before winning!</i>

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:20.070
<i>I guess I'll analyze her inside 
and out during the semifinals</i>

00:08:20.070 --> 00:08:22.190
<i>so we can beat the snot 
out of her in the finals!</i>

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:24.560
Pon.

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:28.010
<i>Two calls. One more.</i>

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:29.760
<i>In the second round match,</i>

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:32.150
<i>it was safe until she had 
called three times...</i>

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:34.770
<i>If you focus too much on not 
letting her call your tiles,</i>

00:08:34.770 --> 00:08:36.320
<i>you'll limit your own hand.</i>

00:08:37.210 --> 00:08:38.750
<i>I guess there's just no denying</i>

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:40.350
<i>that she's a regular at Shiraitodai.</i>

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:41.500
Pon.

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:44.950
<i>Hit.</i>

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:47.420
<i>Three calls!</i>

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:50.180
<i>If this is like her match history,</i>

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:51.800
<i>she'll draw her winning 
tile within five turns!</i>

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:53.170
<i>I have to win first!</i>

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:54.310
<i>Can't we stop her?</i>

00:08:57.620 --> 00:09:00.000
Tsumo. 2,000. 4,000.

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:01.660
<i>One turn!</i>

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:03.300
<i>The dealer penalty hurts...</i>

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:07.900
The first win comes from 
Shiraitodai's Matano Seiko!

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:09.900
East Hand 2

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:10.900
<i>Now...</i>

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:14.090
<i>This hand, tanyao and pinfu,</i>

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:16.910
<i>add a dora or riichi, 
and I can get three han.</i>

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:20.660
<i>Reservation! Three!</i>

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:27.790
Marvelous

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:28.600
<i>Marvelous!</i>

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:31.370
<i>Three spots, limiting to three han...</i>

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:35.630
<i>Next, we have Shindouji's pair.</i>

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:38.550
<i>Tsuruhime and Shirouzu, 
that's the one, right?</i>

00:09:39.230 --> 00:09:41.250
<i>Where their wins are linked?</i>

00:09:41.630 --> 00:09:42.820
<i>What's that?</i>

00:09:42.820 --> 00:09:47.150
<i>Tsuruta Himeko always plays 
right after Shirouzu Mairu.</i>

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:50.200
<i>Her wins have double the han.</i>

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:53.480
<i>For instance, Shirouzu wins a</i>

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:57.240
<i>two han tanyao pinfu for 2,000 points 
in East Hand 3, with two han,</i>

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:57.150
East Hand 3

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:57.150
2 Han

00:09:57.670 --> 00:09:59.100
<i>then Tsuruhime will win with a</i>

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:01.530
East Hand 3

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:01.450
<i>mangan with four han in her East Hand 3.</i>

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:01.530
4 Han

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:07.080
South Hands         East Hands

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:04.150
<i>The rounds where Shirouzu doesn't win,</i>

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:07.080
Han

00:10:04.150 --> 00:10:06.270
<i>Tsuruhime often can't win either.</i>

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:10.390
<i>These two did quite well in 
the middle school tournament</i>

00:10:10.390 --> 00:10:11.960
<i>three years ago, didn't they?</i>

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:14.170
<i>There were some hands that 
didn't follow the pattern,</i>

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:15.990
<i>so it was hard to figure out.</i>

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:17.930
<i>Then Teru figured it out</i>

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:19.460
<i>with her mirror in the 
Spring tournament.</i>

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:24.330
<i>First, Shirouzu-san looks 
at her starting hand</i>

00:10:24.330 --> 00:10:26.140
<i>and puts a limit on herself.</i>

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:28.290
<i>Like, "at least two han," 
or "at least three han."</i>

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:30.910
<i>If she is able to win that hand,</i>

00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:32.610
<i>Tsuruta-san wins with twice</i>

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:34.940
<i>the han in the same hand in the next match.</i>

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:38.530
<i>So that means, if she 
limits herself and wins,</i>

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:40.830
<i>her partner gets a good hand?</i>

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:42.620
<i>Yes. But...</i>

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:45.550
<i>if she limits herself and does not win,</i>

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:48.560
<i>Tsuruta-san can almost 
never win in that hand.</i>

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:51.070
<i>She might very occasionally 
win, but then it seems</i>

00:10:51.070 --> 00:10:52.630
<i>she can't get higher than 1 han.</i>

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:57.850
<i>Shirouzu-san decides if and 
how she limits herself</i>

00:10:57.850 --> 00:11:00.120
<i>after looking at her starting hand.</i>

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:03.930
<i>If she doesn't limit herself, 
they're not linked,</i>

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:05.510
<i>and their wins and points 
are totally disconnected.</i>

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:08.400
<i>Is it possible for anybody to tell?</i>

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:11.880
<i>No. She puts her tiles back down once.</i>

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:13.870
<i>It seems that that move is necessary,</i>

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:15.200
<i>but she does it every time.</i>

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:16.780
<i>How careful of her.</i>

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:20.110
<i>And, unlike regular limits,</i>

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:22.230
<i>she isn't limited to the 
han value of the yaku,</i>

00:11:22.230 --> 00:11:24.390
<i>but can include dora in the count, too.</i>

00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:25.930
<i>What? That's so cheap!</i>

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:30.200
<i>Well, whatever, that's 
none of my concern.</i>

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:32.760
<i>That's something Awai 
has to watch out for.</i>

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:33.880
<i>All I have to do is...</i>

00:11:34.450 --> 00:11:35.040
Pon!

00:11:36.580 --> 00:11:38.840
<i>Keep winning!</i>

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:39.670
Ron.

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:41.470
2,000.

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:45.390
<i>Honestly, it's like I'm not 
even on your radar.</i>

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:47.850
<i>If you think too little of me, 
I'll make you go bust,</i>

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:50.850
<i>regardless of the data!</i>

00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:53.350
<i>She aimed for my pon discard?</i>

00:11:55.030 --> 00:11:58.770
<i>This hand didn't work out.
 Sorry, Himeko...</i>

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:07.030
<i>It's a bit lonely, being left out like this.</i>

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:09.940
<i>Oh well, from here on...</i>

00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:16.880
Kiyosumi's semifinal match is tomorrow, 
so don't go overboard.

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:18.800
But of course!

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:26.690
Someone's sleeping there...

00:12:26.690 --> 00:12:28.300
Wait, Miyanaga-san?

00:12:28.300 --> 00:12:29.260
It's Saki!

00:12:29.690 --> 00:12:31.510
Nobody else is here.

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:36.980
Wake up!

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:39.940
Water surface... fish...

00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:42.950
Looks like she's deep 
in the dreamland.

00:12:43.290 --> 00:12:46.450
That's torture for anyone 
who's not a morning person.

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:45.680
Saki! Saki!

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:48.260
We came to play!

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:54.740
Koromo-chan?

00:12:56.550 --> 00:12:58.340
Nonoka isn't here?

00:12:59.580 --> 00:13:02.860
She went to the tournament hall to 
watch her childhood friend play.

00:13:04.060 --> 00:13:06.300
A childhood friend in the other block...

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:08.260
That's kinda nice.

00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:09.150
Yeah.

00:13:09.570 --> 00:13:12.780
I went up to the entrance as well,

00:13:12.780 --> 00:13:15.440
but then I called to cancel and came home.

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:18.270
Saki, you're just as unsociable as always.

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:19.510
You think so?

00:13:19.510 --> 00:13:22.760
Hey, do you think 
Haramura-san's childhood friend

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:24.030
is from that place?

00:13:26.340 --> 00:13:27.850
Achiga Girls'!

00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:28.570
You know her?

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:32.960
We had a training match, 
about two months back.

00:13:33.480 --> 00:13:35.920
When we got the request for the match,

00:13:35.920 --> 00:13:40.440
I thought that there weren't many 
schools stronger than Kiyosumi.

00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:44.840
It looks like we ended up making 
your opponents stronger, Saki...

00:13:45.270 --> 00:13:48.900
Don't worry, it's more fun to 
play against strong people.

00:13:48.900 --> 00:13:49.720
Actually,

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:53.780
Achiga's fifth player is a bit problematic.

00:13:56.800 --> 00:13:57.900
Arata-san...

00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:01.230
Shizu. Time to warm up!

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:02.020
Okay!

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:05.170
Let's push you up a 
gear before you start.

00:14:05.590 --> 00:14:08.270
Why not set her two gears higher, then?

00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:12.370
Actually, I don't know what that 
means, but please do ten gears!

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:14.700
Ten gears?

00:14:15.110 --> 00:14:16.210
Shizu-chan...

00:14:16.570 --> 00:14:17.370
<i>Ten...</i>

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:21.250
<i>Arata-san! Just unleash 
whatever you've got!</i>

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:24.050
<i>I'll take care of the rest!</i>

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:31.770
East Hand 2 Bonus 1

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:33.220
<i>A bonus...</i>

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:36.980
Shindouji Girls' (Fukuoka)
3rd Year - Fourth player
 Shirouzu Mairu

00:14:33.650 --> 00:14:38.100
<i>I don't know if this bonus hand 
will exist in the fifth players' match,</i>

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:40.500
<i>but still, Himeko might 
have that chance.</i>

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:43.590
<i>Reservation! Two!</i>

00:14:44.810 --> 00:14:47.740
<i>I'm going to win this hand with two han!</i>

00:14:49.440 --> 00:14:49.950
Pon!

00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:52.660
<i>Bring it on!</i>

00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:53.780
Chi!

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:55.410
<i>Both their hands are fast.</i>

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:57.540
<i>It's just pon and chi.</i>

00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:01.860
<i>Pon.</i>

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:09.230
<i>Yum. Your data is so tasty.</i>

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:12.400
<i>I'll bleed every last bit of it out of you.</i>

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:16.100
<i>The others are kind of running 
wild, but my draws are good.</i>

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:18.270
<i>Oh, this is ba—</i>

00:15:18.690 --> 00:15:19.440
Pon.

00:15:21.550 --> 00:15:22.560
<i>I won't let you fish it!</i>

00:15:25.840 --> 00:15:27.560
Ron! 2,300!

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:29.880
<i>Reservation cleared!</i>

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:42.580
<i>I got a mangan key.</i>

00:15:43.220 --> 00:15:45.430
<i>Nicely done, President!</i>

00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:48.210
<i>I cleared one...</i>

00:15:48.690 --> 00:15:51.780
<i>but it's a key for Bonus 1 of East Hand 2.</i>

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:55.080
<i>If that hand never happens 
in her match, it's useless.</i>

00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:57.340
<i>I'm afraid that key won't be used.</i>

00:15:57.770 --> 00:16:00.730
<i>I'm going to get more! I'll be greedy!</i>

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:03.120
<i>Two han, no...</i>

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:06.480
<i>Reservation! Four!</i>

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:12.820
Huh? It's a big one?

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:16.450
Yes, probably four han...

00:16:16.690 --> 00:16:19.860
Marvelous!
 The challenge of a four han limit

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:21.540
against speedy Matano.

00:16:22.010 --> 00:16:23.480
That's our president!

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:25.750
Tsumo!

00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:27.500
2,000. 4,000.

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:31.760
<i>Reservation cleared!</i>

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:39.350
<i>East Hand 3, baiman key!</i>

00:16:40.300 --> 00:16:42.860
<i>If she had limited herself,
 it was three or four.</i>

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:46.150
<i>Awai will have to be 
prepared for a baiman.</i>

00:16:47.760 --> 00:16:49.980
They can have a baiman if they want.

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:53.290
Last year, Shindouji put their ace in first

00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:55.920
and other heavy hitters in the middle:

00:16:55.920 --> 00:16:57.320
a very offense-oriented order.

00:16:57.320 --> 00:16:59.220
However, this year they 
changed their strategy!

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:02.410
It was a good idea to 
put their two aces in last.

00:17:02.850 --> 00:17:05.990
There are barely any teams who have 
their ace as the fourth player.

00:17:05.990 --> 00:17:09.920
That's exactly why I think 
Shirouzu is suited for that slot.

00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:12.670
<i>This way, she can win more 
often instead of getting</i>

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:14.930
<i>caught up in the ace 
battle in the beginning.</i>

00:17:15.140 --> 00:17:16.930
Ah, I see.

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:18.930
What? You didn't know?!

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:22.590
East Hand 4

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:24.430
Ron. 7,700.

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:25.580
Okay.

00:17:26.180 --> 00:17:28.150
<i>I was thinking this in the 
second round match, too,</i>

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:30.670
<i>but Shirouzu Mairu really is tough.</i>

00:17:31.390 --> 00:17:35.530
<i>Shiraitodai's number 5 can 
surpass prefectural aces.</i>

00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:38.830
<i>That's something I have 
personally experienced.</i>

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:43.290
<i>However, Shirouzu Mairu 
isn't just some ace.</i>

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:47.920
East Hand 4

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:47.920
Bonus 1

00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:48.670
<i>She's been the ace of the strongest 
high school in north Kyushu for three years...</i>

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:50.170
<i>a true ace!</i>

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:53.050
Third Turn

00:17:52.410 --> 00:17:53.050
Pon.

00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:57.180
Pon.

00:17:59.110 --> 00:18:02.350
<i>Fisherlady, I'm glad you're to my left.</i>

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:04.100
<i>That way I can take the hand lead again...</i>

00:18:04.450 --> 00:18:05.220
Riichi!

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:05.770
Pon.

00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:09.020
<i>She caught up to me!</i>

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:12.210
Riichi.

00:18:12.710 --> 00:18:15.180
<i>Achiga... Sagimori Arata?!</i>

00:18:24.510 --> 00:18:27.410
Tsumo. 3,100. 6,100.

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:30.480
<i>On top of the dealer 
penalty for the haneman,</i>

00:18:30.480 --> 00:18:32.040
<i>she took my riichi wager, too...</i>

00:18:32.430 --> 00:18:35.610
<i>Sagimori... So she was 
this kind of player.</i>

00:18:36.350 --> 00:18:37.570
<i>A Greek Church!</i>

00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:40.050
<i>Her wait was for a 4, 6, 7, or 9 of circles.</i>

00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:42.800
South Hand 1

00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:42.800
Dealer Sagimori Arata

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:43.200
<i>I don't have much data on her,</i>

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:45.790
<i>but Sagimori's waits are often circles.</i>

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:49.560
<i>Most of the time, they're similar to 
specially named splits in bowling.</i>

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:56.130
<i>With 4, 6, 7, 9, 10 left, it's 
a Greek Church or Big Five.</i>

00:18:56.590 --> 00:18:59.660
<i>Well, there's no 10 of circles in mahjong.</i>

00:19:00.400 --> 00:19:03.300
<i>For instance, a wait for 
a 1, 2, or 4 of circles</i>

00:19:03.300 --> 00:19:05.410
<i>is like the Washout in bowling.</i>

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:09.270
<i>But I don't know if such a dynamic, 
fanciful theory has any merit...</i>

00:19:09.770 --> 00:19:12.250
<i>One more thing, her 
style is old-fashioned.</i>

00:19:12.740 --> 00:19:16.010
<i>Either she played a long 
time ago and had a hiatus,</i>

00:19:16.610 --> 00:19:18.960
<i>or she looks up to someone 
from the old days...</i>

00:19:20.790 --> 00:19:21.540
Tsumo.

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:23.580
2,000. 4,000.

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:26.790
<i>She stealthed that one, so 
she's focusing on winning.</i>

00:19:26.790 --> 00:19:29.180
<i>Does that mean she set 
a limit below 3 han?</i>

00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:32.390
<i>I do accept that you're 
in a higher class,</i>

00:19:32.390 --> 00:19:34.740
<i>but you're winning too 
much, ye of Fukuoka!</i>

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:36.440
South Hand 2

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:36.440
Dealer Funakubo Hiroko

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:40.420
<i>Huh? My attempt at a pinfu ippeikou 
turned into a chiitoitsu.</i>

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:40.420
[iipeikou - double sequence in the same suit 2-3-4 / 2-3-4]
[chiitoitsu - 7 pairs]

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:45.050
<i>There are no honor tiles left that 
someone would be waiting for,</i>

00:19:45.050 --> 00:19:47.420
<i>this could be a good time to use 
the discarded suji as a trap.</i>

00:19:45.050 --> 00:19:47.420
[Suji - Tiles that are 3 apart, completing a sequence; 
ex: 3/6/9. Other players may use suji in 
discards to determine safer tiles.]

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:51.290
<i>Most importantly, I'm the dealer... 
I guess I'll go for it.</i>

00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:52.580
Riichi.

00:19:53.690 --> 00:19:55.020
<i>A dealer riichi.</i>

00:19:58.370 --> 00:19:59.980
<i>Looks like Matano is out.</i>

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:04.990
<i>I have this kind of hand against a 
dealer riichi this late in the game...</i>

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:07.050
<i>Normally, I'd be out too,</i>

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:09.600
<i>but I won't back down!</i>

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:13.060
<i>My wins can't be measured 
by normal expectation values!</i>

00:20:13.950 --> 00:20:14.650
Riichi!

00:20:15.470 --> 00:20:18.530
<i>They become the wins 
of Himeko and myself!</i>

00:20:20.140 --> 00:20:22.680
<i>Hasn't this girl gained enough yet?</i>

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:27.280
<i>I'd like to stay offensive while 
playing it somewhat safe...</i>

00:20:30.590 --> 00:20:31.870
<i>Maybe this?</i>

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:36.260
Ron. 9,600.

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:38.760
Okay.

00:20:40.130 --> 00:20:41.390
<i>A suji trap?!</i>

00:20:42.860 --> 00:20:44.430
<i>She dealt into her hand!</i>

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:49.470
Matano has a habit of relying too much on 
suji and honor tiles when she plays it safe.

00:20:50.050 --> 00:20:52.330
I suppose she usually wins with that,

00:20:52.330 --> 00:20:55.730
but this time her opponents are 
Shirouzu, who's a grade above,

00:20:56.170 --> 00:20:58.730
and her, who I'm afraid 
is using that weakness.

00:20:59.970 --> 00:21:00.610
Ron.

00:21:01.540 --> 00:21:03.570
12,300.

00:21:05.650 --> 00:21:08.020
<i>An honor tile that was just discarded twice?!</i>

00:21:10.220 --> 00:21:12.330
<i>That was yummy.</i>

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:15.210
Looking good.

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:17.130
Coach? When did you get here?!

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:20.880
Senriyama Girls' (North Osaka)
 Coach
 Atago Masae

00:21:17.430 --> 00:21:20.870
I left Toki in the care 
of Izumi and Ryuuka.

00:21:21.370 --> 00:21:23.010
Why don't you go to the hospital, too?

00:21:23.210 --> 00:21:26.510
No, it'd be sad if no regular was here

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:29.010
when FunaQ comes back.

00:21:29.200 --> 00:21:31.800
Oh, by FunaQ, I mean Hiroko.

00:21:31.800 --> 00:21:33.920
I know, no problem.

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:36.610
She's doing quite well.

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:38.600
I'm really glad.

00:21:39.160 --> 00:21:41.290
I don't want anybody 
to say I pulled her in

00:21:41.290 --> 00:21:43.030
because she's my niece.

00:21:43.400 --> 00:21:45.150
For her sake as well...

00:21:45.740 --> 00:21:48.160
Everybody in the club knows that,

00:21:48.180 --> 00:21:53.160
<b>Focus completely on one single endeavor</b>

00:21:49.060 --> 00:21:51.280
but I guess it can't be 
helped that only results

00:21:51.280 --> 00:21:52.770
matter to the outside.

00:21:53.650 --> 00:21:56.270
<i>FunaQ should be aware of that, too.</i>

00:21:53.700 --> 00:21:56.160
South Hand 2

00:21:53.700 --> 00:21:56.160
Bonus 2

00:21:57.370 --> 00:22:01.210
<i>600 points left to Achiga, 
in second place.</i>

00:22:03.010 --> 00:22:04.370
<i>I can almost reach her...</i>

00:22:05.960 --> 00:22:06.960
<i>I got her!</i>

00:22:07.630 --> 00:22:08.390
Riichi.

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:11.850
<i>What? The riichi wager?!</i>

00:22:12.520 --> 00:22:14.360
<i>Oh well, second place is second place.</i>

00:22:14.360 --> 00:22:16.060
<i>My plan to get to second 
place is a success!</i>

00:22:16.750 --> 00:22:19.220
<i>All right, first I'll have 
to stop her from winning!</i>

00:22:19.970 --> 00:22:23.570
<i>With Sagimori Arata, anything 
but circles should be safe!</i>

00:22:23.790 --> 00:22:26.450
...is something that they 
might be thinking,

00:22:26.880 --> 00:22:28.420
but just you watch.

00:22:30.700 --> 00:22:31.450
Ron!

00:22:34.690 --> 00:22:35.890
8,600!

00:22:36.300 --> 00:22:37.370
<i>Waiting for a 9 of characters?!</i>

00:22:37.670 --> 00:22:38.830
<i>What the...</i>

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:40.080
<i>This...</i>

00:22:41.640 --> 00:22:47.540
<i>She threw away her 4, 6, 7 of circles 
Big Four wait for a 9 of characters wait?!</i>

00:22:47.540 --> 00:22:50.090
<i>If you have a good hand, why don't 
you just go for a tsumo win?!</i>

00:22:58.140 --> 00:23:00.480
Because you look like you're 
the most level headed.

00:23:00.900 --> 00:23:02.810
Me? Level headed?

00:23:02.810 --> 00:23:03.540
Yup.

00:23:04.520 --> 00:23:05.900
That's why I'm the club president?

00:23:05.900 --> 00:23:06.860
Righto.

00:23:08.510 --> 00:23:13.930
But if you're talking about level headed, 
I think Ako-chan's level headed, too.

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:21.050
Well, I think Ako's "level headed" 
has a different vector.

00:23:21.050 --> 00:23:23.510
Sometimes she's more "sharp minded" 
than "level headed," you know?

00:23:23.510 --> 00:23:25.130
You might be right about that.

00:23:25.590 --> 00:23:29.380
Plus, for this, looking 
"level headed" is also important.

00:23:30.250 --> 00:23:32.390
So appearance is an important factor.

00:23:34.070 --> 00:23:36.640
If you say so, I'll do it.

00:23:37.310 --> 00:23:39.870
Really? That's great!

00:23:40.400 --> 00:23:43.250
I was actually the club president, too.

00:23:43.250 --> 00:23:44.650
I was a first year, though.

00:23:48.170 --> 00:23:49.280
<i>I knew that.</i>

00:23:50.890 --> 00:23:53.650
<i>What I didn't know was 
the weight that carried...</i>

00:23:56.770 --> 00:23:58.040
President!

00:23:58.350 --> 00:24:00.340
Give it your best, Pres!

00:24:00.340 --> 00:24:02.280
Looking cheap, Mr. President!

00:24:02.280 --> 00:24:03.380
That's not...

00:24:05.980 --> 00:24:09.470
<i>The expectations of many people... 
the responsibility...</i>

00:24:10.300 --> 00:24:11.430
<i>L-Listen!</i>

00:24:12.150 --> 00:24:15.430
<i>If you embarrass yourselves at the 
Nationals, I won't forgive you!</i>

00:24:15.450 --> 00:24:17.390
<b>Achiga Girls' 
Fan Club Head Office</b>

00:24:17.880 --> 00:24:23.150
<i>I'd like to thank you for 
gathering here today.</i>

00:24:24.590 --> 00:24:25.770
<i>Hey!</i>

00:24:26.120 --> 00:24:27.700
<i>Wh-What a coincidence!</i>

00:24:28.010 --> 00:24:28.780
<i>What is it?</i>

00:24:29.410 --> 00:24:33.060
<i>Y-You guys have some time next week?</i>

00:24:33.480 --> 00:24:35.410
<i>Scary, I don't know what you're after...</i>

00:24:35.410 --> 00:24:38.460
<i>I'm telling you that we'll 
do a send-off game for you!</i>

00:24:38.460 --> 00:24:40.380
<i>That's Bansei, including 
myself, the number one</i>

00:24:40.380 --> 00:24:41.920
<i>in Nara's individual tournament!</i>

00:24:41.920 --> 00:24:44.170
<i>That would be really helpful...</i>

00:24:44.230 --> 00:24:46.440
Win at Nationals!!

00:24:47.200 --> 00:24:48.470
<i>The things entrusted to me...</i>

00:24:49.790 --> 00:24:53.850
<i>Right now, I'm here with 
the feelings of many people.</i>

00:24:56.110 --> 00:24:59.660
<i>I wonder if Haru-chan 
felt like this, too?</i>

00:25:01.920 --> 00:25:05.720
<i>Back then, I had entrusted 
Haru-chan with my feelings.</i>

00:25:06.950 --> 00:25:07.970
<i>But now...</i>

00:25:08.870 --> 00:25:10.300
<i>I'm the one carrying them,</i>

00:25:11.050 --> 00:25:12.880
<i>along with the feelings of many others,</i>

00:25:13.870 --> 00:25:15.260
<i>the feelings of that person...</i>

00:25:19.200 --> 00:25:21.000
Tsumo. 2,000. 4,000.

00:25:21.370 --> 00:25:23.960
<i>It's Sagimori Arata again!</i>

00:25:24.230 --> 00:25:28.910
<i>The gap between her and Shiraitodai 
in first place is 11,300 points!</i>

00:25:28.910 --> 00:25:31.960
<i>A direct mangan hit could put her on top!</i>

00:25:32.800 --> 00:25:34.420
<i>Since I became a regular,</i>

00:25:34.420 --> 00:25:37.900
<i>I've never fallen into second in the 
fourth players' match, not even once...</i>

00:25:38.590 --> 00:25:41.070
<i>I've never lost so many points, either!</i>

00:25:41.640 --> 00:25:44.480
<i>Who are these two who aren't Shirouzu?!</i>

00:25:45.020 --> 00:25:47.540
<i>She wasn't like this up to 
the second round match.</i>

00:25:48.080 --> 00:25:51.230
<i>I guess she transformed here 
like the third years do</i>

00:25:51.230 --> 00:25:54.560
<i>during the Inter High tournaments...</i>

00:25:55.050 --> 00:25:58.920
<i>It's like she has a special sentiment 
towards the semifinals, or something.</i>

00:26:00.860 --> 00:26:03.830
Now, the fourth players' match 
is drawing to a close.

00:26:03.120 --> 00:26:05.120
Second Half

00:26:03.120 --> 00:26:05.120
South Hand 3

00:26:03.830 --> 00:26:05.900
South Hand 3
of the second half!

00:26:05.140 --> 00:26:06.750
Shiraitodai High School (West Tokyo)
 2nd year - Fourth player
 Matano Seiko

00:26:05.900 --> 00:26:08.020
Matano lost many points 
in the first half,

00:26:06.940 --> 00:26:08.620
Achiga Girls' (Nara)
 2nd Year - Fourth Player
 Sagimori Arata

00:26:08.020 --> 00:26:09.750
but she still has a chance!

00:26:08.770 --> 00:26:10.500
Senriyama Girls' (North Osaka)
 2nd Year - Fourth Player
 Funakubo Hiroko

00:26:09.750 --> 00:26:12.170
She's not conceding the throne just yet!

00:26:10.650 --> 00:26:12.550
Shindouji Girls' (Fukuoka)
 3rd Year - Fourth Player
 Shirouzu Mairu

00:26:13.150 --> 00:26:17.160
<i>I've gained quite a few 
points, but it's not enough.</i>

00:26:17.750 --> 00:26:20.760
<i>But this starting hand...</i>

00:26:22.540 --> 00:26:24.650
<i>Five? Or six?</i>

00:26:25.310 --> 00:26:26.050
<i>No!</i>

00:26:27.580 --> 00:26:28.770
<i>Reservation!</i>

00:26:29.700 --> 00:26:30.590
<i>Seven!</i>

00:26:33.570 --> 00:26:35.740
<i>Seven han, now?</i>

00:26:36.230 --> 00:26:38.490
<i>That's a bit reckless, President...</i>

00:26:39.010 --> 00:26:40.580
<i>With normal opponents,</i>

00:26:40.580 --> 00:26:43.490
<i>winning with a couple of 
3,900 hands was easy.</i>

00:26:43.780 --> 00:26:48.250
<i>But with this point difference, 
that won't be enough!</i>

00:26:48.530 --> 00:26:50.540
<i>I'll have to be reckless here!</i>

00:26:51.130 --> 00:26:53.460
<i>It can't be helped that 
Shirouzu is strong,</i>

00:26:54.310 --> 00:26:58.710
<i>but I feel like Sagimori Arata 
has become a serious problem.</i>

00:26:59.580 --> 00:27:04.140
<i>Partially due to the ridiculous luck 
of that Kentani first year,</i>

00:27:04.140 --> 00:27:06.310
<i>the lack of research is really showing.</i>

00:27:07.490 --> 00:27:08.810
<i>This is throwing me for a loop.</i>

00:27:09.240 --> 00:27:11.480
<i>If her waits are not limited to circles,</i>

00:27:11.480 --> 00:27:14.110
<i>all that means is that I need 
to play carefully, as usual.</i>

00:27:15.040 --> 00:27:16.990
<i>Still, it feels like I'm 
being strung around...</i>

00:27:18.000 --> 00:27:21.060
<i>I can't shake the feeling 
that you have the</i>

00:27:21.060 --> 00:27:22.950
<i>scent of a previous 
generation, Sagimori.</i>

00:27:23.700 --> 00:27:25.200
<i>Previous generation?</i>

00:27:27.450 --> 00:27:31.110
<i>That's it! Achiga Girls' 
coach, Akado Harue!</i>

00:27:31.110 --> 00:27:33.290
<i>What's more, it's her old style!</i>

00:27:34.160 --> 00:27:38.090
<i>I did glance at the records 
of each school's advisors,</i>

00:27:38.090 --> 00:27:42.320
<i>but obviously the focus was 
on the current players.</i>

00:27:42.320 --> 00:27:46.400
<i>Still, Sagimori Arata has 
suddenly started to mix her</i>

00:27:46.400 --> 00:27:49.590
<i>coach's old style into her own 
"circles multi-sided wait" style,</i>

00:27:49.590 --> 00:27:50.790
<i>during the semifinals.</i>

00:27:51.560 --> 00:27:52.930
<i>It's taken me a while,</i>

00:27:52.930 --> 00:27:55.520
<i>but I'm finally starting to 
see what's behind Achiga.</i>

00:27:56.240 --> 00:27:58.080
<i>The sentiments towards the semifinals,</i>

00:27:58.750 --> 00:28:01.460
<i>the strong will the pupils are 
mustering for their teacher...</i>

00:28:02.090 --> 00:28:03.660
<i>This is revenge ten 
years in the making!</i>

00:28:07.150 --> 00:28:07.970
Riichi!

00:28:07.760 --> 00:28:09.140
Eighth Turn

00:28:09.500 --> 00:28:11.710
<i>Shindouji, you're seriously still going?!</i>

00:28:12.250 --> 00:28:14.040
<i>Her discards suggest she 
has a characters-only hand.</i>

00:28:14.900 --> 00:28:17.740
<i>If you declare riichi, those 
won't come out any more...</i>

00:28:18.970 --> 00:28:21.630
<i>Did she really put a high 
limit on and declare riichi</i>

00:28:21.630 --> 00:28:23.800
<i>with the intention of drawing 
the winning tile herself?!</i>

00:28:26.050 --> 00:28:26.810
Riichi!

00:28:28.860 --> 00:28:30.430
<i>Achiga's caught up!</i>

00:28:30.930 --> 00:28:33.110
<i>For a 7 or 9 of circles, Cincinnati.</i>

00:28:33.590 --> 00:28:35.480
<i>I'll hand this over in first place.</i>

00:28:35.740 --> 00:28:38.310
<i>For Haru-chan and everybody!</i>

00:28:44.540 --> 00:28:48.660
I can't believe it! Shirouzu 
ignores the cheaper win!

00:28:53.310 --> 00:28:53.960
Tsumo!

00:28:55.250 --> 00:28:57.380
<i>Reservation Seven, cleared!</i>

00:28:57.970 --> 00:28:59.460
4,000. 8,000.

00:28:59.780 --> 00:29:01.720
A baiman tsumo!

00:29:02.200 --> 00:29:05.470
<i>She ignored my winning tile 
and got a baiman tsumo?</i>

00:29:06.100 --> 00:29:09.470
<i>If Tsuruta Himeko wins double this...</i>

00:29:10.080 --> 00:29:13.600
It's fine, you can have a "counted" one.

00:29:19.270 --> 00:29:20.830
A 14-han key...

00:29:42.010 --> 00:29:58.000
<b>Intensify</b>

00:29:42.870 --> 00:29:44.190
I'm late, I'm late!

00:29:44.190 --> 00:29:45.160
Shizu, watch out!

00:29:45.160 --> 00:29:48.680
Phew, got it!
 I almost dropped my bread!

00:29:48.680 --> 00:29:50.610
Jeez, Shizu, you're such a slob.

00:29:50.610 --> 00:29:52.400
Chew that bread and finish it already.

00:29:52.400 --> 00:29:54.730
And you have to be careful 
when you turn a corner.

00:29:54.730 --> 00:29:55.770
Okay.
